  "headline": "Home of the Taj Mahal",
  "short_description": "Agra's Mughal-era monuments, above all the Taj Mahal, make it one of the most visited cities in India.",
  "about": "Once the capital of the Mughal Empire under Akbar, Jahangir and Shah Jahan, Agra is best known worldwide for the Taj Mahal but holds a wider cluster of Mughal architecture along the Yamuna.\n\nSituated on the banks of the Yamuna river in western Uttar Pradesh.\n\nA centre of Mughal architecture, marble inlay (pietra dura) craftsmanship and leather goods.\n\nPredominantly Hindu and Muslim population; Mughal-era mosques stand alongside temples.",
  "history": "Agra rose to prominence as the Mughal capital in the 16th–17th centuries, producing the Agra Fort and the Taj Mahal, before the capital shifted to Delhi.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Agra Airport (airport)\n- Agra Cantt Railway Station (railway)\n- Idgah Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, English (tourist areas)\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "1–2 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Agra Airport (AGR), limited service; most visitors fly via Delhi",
  "nearest_railway_station": "Agra Cantt Railway Station",
